          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life</strong><br>\nLeon Trotsky was born Lev Davidovich Bronstein in Yanovka, Ukraine, in 1879. He grew up in a Jewish farming family, and at an early age, he became involved in underground revolutionary activities, leading to multiple arrests.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Marxist Beliefs and Activities</strong><br>\nTrotsky became a Marxist during his early years and played a key role in the 1905 Saint Petersburg Soviet's activities. He developed his theory of \"permanent revolution,\" which would later become a central tenet of Trotskyism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Role in the 1917 Revolution</strong><br>\nDuring the Russian Revolution of 1917, Trotsky was a significant figure in the Bolshevik party. He played a leading role in the October Revolution, which led to the Bolsheviks' rise to power.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
