          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Commissar of Foreign Affairs</strong><br>\nAfter the Bolsheviks gained control, Trotsky served as the People's Commissar for Foreign Affairs. In this role, he negotiated the Brest-Litovsk peace treaty with Germany to end Russia's involvement in World War I.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Founding the Red Army</strong><br>\nTrotsky founded and led the Red Army during the Russian Civil War. His leadership was crucial in defending the Bolshevik government against various opposition forces.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Power Struggle and Exile</strong><br>\nAfter Lenin's death, Trotsky lost a power struggle to Joseph Stalin. He was exiled in 1929 and spent the rest of his life criticizing Stalin's leadership and the direction of the Soviet Union.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
